<title>UK: BAA shares rise in traffic figure follow-up.</title>
<headline>BAA shares rise in traffic figure follow-up.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in BAA Plc rose 17p  to 584-1/2 on Friday, still boosted by Thursday's release of favourable traffic figures for the airports operated by BAA.</p>
<p>The company reported it achieved passenger growth of 8.9 percent in its seven airports, including London's Heathrow, while cargo rose by 6.5 percent to 131,031 tonnes in May.</p>
<p>BAA shares will go ex-dividend on Monday and dealers cited this as another reason for today's buying interest.</p>
<p>BAA on June 9 announced a final dividend of 7.9 pence per share.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
